uarantee keeps Medi-Cal and the private insurance market, which rules out rung 5.\n- **Rung 2 is not reached.** No passage says everyone should have coverage.\n- **Rung 3 is not reached.** His spending plan narrows Medi-Cal rather than expanding it: it ends state-funded coverage for undocumented immigrants and changes asset limits and premiums. That works against rung 3's \"expand programs\".\n- **Rung 4 is not reached.** Nothing says help should go only to the poorest. He also proposes reinsurance for the individual market, aimed at working families.\n\n**Which passages carried the blank:** the two dated debate answers (2026-09-30 and 2026-05-29) and the 2025-11-20 interview. All three are from the current campaign.\n\n**Judgment calls you may want to check:**\n- **Undated own-site pages.** The campaign policy pages print no date, so I coded them `undated`, which means they cannot support a chair. This does not change the result here, because the dated debate answers support the same blank, but another coder may treat a live campaign page as current-campaign instead.\n- **Interview class.** I coded the November 2025 interview as `statement-other`, not `statement-answer`, because the codebook lists interviews under `statement-other`.\n\n**Other passages:** the Medi-Cal fraud page is `adjacent`. The new-cities and anti-corruption pages are `off`. The OnTheIssues page is a pointer and not evidence.\n\n`needs_source` is empty; I found nothing missing that would decide the row.\n\n**Quotes:** I tiered six. Three are `lever` with `lever-named`: the Section 1332 waiver, the personal healthcare accounts, and ending Medi-Cal for undocumented immigrants. Two are `direction`: the two \"affordable premium, low deductible\" guarantee lines. The single-payer line is `none` and marked not quotable as `not-forward`, since it is a criticism rather than what he would do.","ttft_ms":20071,"type":"result","duration_ms":57012,"uuid":"19886500-467b-41e9-9237-bbfe0d6c6ac6","ttft_stream_m